docs/ENHANCEMENTS.md:27:- OAuth for MCP clients (the MCP authorization spec), so users connect by signing in instead of pasting a token. Its access tokens plug in as one more `RequestAuthenticator`; the MCP TypeScript SDK's auth helpers cover the authorization-server endpoints.
docs/ENHANCEMENTS.md:47:- MCP dedupe is a lookup before the insert, so two identical `publish_artifact` or `add_comment` calls arriving at the same moment can both go through. Retries come one after another, which it covers; a unique constraint or an advisory lock per `(owner, sha256)` would close the gap.
docs/ENHANCEMENTS.md:65:- The gallery has no "everything I can see" tab, so a search for someone's artifacts picks *Shared with me* or *Company*; one could be in either. An *All* scope (as MCP has) would fix that.
docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:3:A platform for publishing, browsing, reviewing and sharing AI-generated content (HTML, SVG, images, PDFs, Markdown), usable from a web UI and from any MCP client.
docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:14:| Backend | NestJS (REST API + MCP endpoint in the same app) |
docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:17:| Validation | Zod schemas in a shared package, used by API DTOs, web forms and MCP tool schemas |
docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:20:| Auth (MCP) | Per-user API tokens (Bearer), created in the UI and stored hashed |
docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:35:- **Metadata:** title, description and tags are **required** in MCP tools, because the calling LLM has the best context. In the web UI, the form is pre-filled with AI suggestions after upload, and blanks left on submit are filled asynchronously.
docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:58:│  │  │  ├─ uploads/          # upload sessions (MCP binary flow), content validation
docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:64:│  │  │  ├─ mcp/              # MCP server (Streamable HTTP) + intent tools
docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:66:│  │  └─ test/                # e2e (supertest) + MCP client tests
docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:83:**Module boundary rule:** controllers and MCP tools are thin adapters. Both call the same application services (`ArtifactsService`, `SharingService`, `CommentsService`, …). Every service method takes an `Actor` (`{ userId, via: 'web' | 'mcp' }`) and asks `AccessPolicy` before doing anything. The web API and the MCP server therefore cannot drift apart in behaviour or permissions.
docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:106:  status enum('draft','published')           -- draft = awaiting first upload (MCP upload session)
docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:160:One pure-ish service that both REST and MCP use for every decision. Unit-tested exhaustively.
docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:202:The web UI and MCP use the same pipeline:
docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:204:1. **Receive:** multipart with busboy/multer `limits.fileSize = MAX_ARTIFACT_BYTES`, or MCP inline text `content` (byte length checked before processing), or the raw-body `PUT` to an upload session (streamed with the same limit). Anything over the limit gets `413 ARTIFACT_TOO_LARGE`.
docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:207:   - **Text formats** must be UTF-8 throughout, with no NUL bytes (checked as the content streams). Bytes alone can't tell them apart (any text is valid Markdown, and Markdown may contain HTML), so the **extension picks and the content must match**: `.md`/`.markdown` → Markdown (any text); `.html`/`.htm` → HTML (must start with markup); `.svg` → SVG (must have an `<svg>` root; DOCTYPEs with an internal subset are rejected). MCP passes the format explicitly instead of a filename.
docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:235:## 8. MCP server
docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:237:- Uses `@modelcontextprotocol/sdk`, **Streamable HTTP** transport in stateless mode, mounted in Nest at `POST /mcp`.
docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:238:- **Auth:** `Authorization: Bearer <api token>` → `Actor{via:'mcp'}`. Tokens are created on the **Settings → API tokens** page, which also shows a copy-paste Claude Desktop config (the header goes through an env variable because some clients split arguments on spaces) and a `claude mcp add` command for Claude Code:
